From: Pierre Bogdanovscky <pierrebog@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:20:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 19/19] vout: don't drop the picture shown after a seek while
 paused

A flush empties the current picture; while paused, the next one was
prepared with the late check, against a clock that does not run, and
dropped as late by the time spent paused, leaving the old picture.

Work item: #30251

(cherry picked from commit 6127c87a7e5886b476b5223455feae106e6f1e0a)
---
 src/video_output/video_output.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/video_output/video_output.c b/src/video_output/video_output.c
index bde65e65ec..f38548340f 100644
--- a/src/video_output/video_output.c
+++ b/src/video_output/video_output.c
@@ -1602,7 +1602,9 @@ static bool UpdateCurrentPicture(vout_thread_sys_t *sys)
 
     if (sys->displayed.current == NULL)
     {
-        sys->displayed.current = PreparePicture(sys, true, false);
+        /* While paused the clock does not run, so no picture is late: the
+         * first one after a flush, the picture of a seek, must be shown. */
+        sys->displayed.current = PreparePicture(sys, true, sys->pause.is_on);
         return sys->displayed.current != NULL;
     }
 
